Description: Accept IPv6 literals in REDIRECT_DOMAINS
 Without REDIRECT_DOMAINS, pass-challenge redirects a solved challenge to
 any host: it compares the host of redir with itself (lib/anubis.go,
 PassChallenge), an open redirect. Keel Web sets REDIRECT_DOMAINS to the
 machine's names and addresses, as its default site answers by IP too;
 the host of an IPv6 URL is bracketed, [2001:db8::1], and that is what
 Anubis compares, but main refused such an entry at start, as url.Parse
 reads it as a path whose first segment has a colon ("cannot parse
 redirect-domain"). An entry is now accepted when it parses as the host
 of a URL (url.Parse("//" + entry)), or as a URL as before, so nothing
 accepted before is refused. TestParseRedirectDomains covers names,
 addresses, an IPv6 literal, a glob and a refused entry.
